    "number": "OSHPS 16.4",
    "title": "Compressed Air Use",
    "sectionId": "oshps-16-compressed-air",
    "sectionName": "Compressed Air",
    "subsection": "",
    "requirementText": "Compressed Air Use",
    "guidance": [
      "Work rules must be established that that prevent the use of compressed air for the following uses:",
      ">To remove dust or debris from clothing or exposed skin;",
      ">To clean dust in confined spaces, including process equipment enclosures, dust collectors, and false ceiling areas where a hazardous dust cloud could result.",
      "Compressed air hoses must be equipped with wands or nozzles meeting the following requirements:",
      ">Designed hand use and equipped with hand grips",
      ">Equipped with trigger operated air valves that close automatically when there is no pressure on the trigger;",
      ">Equipped with pressure relief holes designed to prevent tip pressures from exceeding 2 bar (30 psi);",
      ">Equipped with air fuses to prevent hose whipping and air releases resulting from hose cuts or nozzle failures.",
      ">Air hoses, connections and air nozzles or guns must be included in the site planned inspection process with a minimum inspection frequency of 6 weeks.",
      ">A pre-use inspection regime is also required to ensure the user checks for damaged hose, gun or loose fittings prior to use.",
      ">Air hoses must be coiled and properly stored when not in use",
      ">Air hoses must not pass through machine guarding.",
      ">Air hoses must be installed with a pressure reducing valve/regulator and an isolating valve capable of being locked in the off position and installed at an easily reachable location at the fixed end of the hose.",
      ">Air hoses must be installed with an air fuse which is used to automatically reduce the air flow and prevent the air hose whipping around if the hose is cut or the air wand breaks free from the hose.",
      "PPE:",
      ">A personal protective equipment (PPE) assessment must be completed for all compressed air tasks. Minimum PPE requirements include safety glasses and hearing protection devices (HPD). Respirators must be used for tasks that create a dust cloud.",
      "Other Pressure Vessels:",
      ">Containers, tires and rim assemblies from motor vehicles, and other pressure vessels must be inspected and in good condition prior to filling them and must not exceed maximum fill pressures"
    ],
    "expectedEvidence": [
      "Planned Inspections: To confirm that compliance controls are effective, planned inspections should be performed with checks connected to Checklists:",
      ">Pre-Use",
      ">Planned Inspection - Planned work observation",
      ">Pressure Vessel Inspections Reports",
      "Documentation: The following compressed air records must be kept:",
      ">System design documents that support the site's compliance status;",
      ">Preventive maintenance of compressed air protection systems and equipment and inspection records; and",
      ">Fugitive dust control and cleaning procedures."
    ],
